            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="0977" n="857" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg857"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.74/253: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-28T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 28,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 28—10:34
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>464. Department’s despatch October 4th.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d655-f1"/> Japanese
                    Minister has filed strong protest against Federal wireless contract.</p>
                <p>Schwerin arrived here 26th. I have had two long conferences with him in which all
                    aspects of matter were discussed and I have assured him that Legation will lend
                    him all possible support.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
